WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.644
Let's follow Alex's birthday dinner through the main FormBridge workspace. This is

00:00:05.644 --> 00:00:11.289
the normal booking desk, with the enquiry book, service planner and desk

00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:12.700
assistant available throughout.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.201
Alex asks for four people at Juniper House in Sydney, on the

00:00:18.201 --> 00:00:23.053
thirteenth of November at seven. The message also mentions a birthday, a

00:00:23.053 --> 00:00:27.500
peanut allergy and a quiet table. Add it to the brief.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:33.507
For an existing enquiry, Paste conversation accepts a single message or a

00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:38.864
labelled customer and staff transcript. It starts a new brief, so keep

00:00:38.864 --> 00:00:40.650
your current enquiry first.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.411
Alex changes the plans by voice. In this example, we upload a

00:00:46.411 --> 00:00:51.522
short recording asking for six guests and sometime after eight. FormBridge transcribes

00:00:51.522 --> 00:00:52.800
it for review.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.686
Read the transcript before putting it into the conversation. Voice input follows

00:00:58.686 --> 00:01:03.050
the same review and extraction flow as a typed message.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.521
The guest count changes to six. After eight stays an unresolved preference.

00:01:08.521 --> 00:01:13.343
The brief asks for an exact time, and the change history keeps

00:01:13.343 --> 00:01:14.950
the earlier details visible.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.727
Open Desk assistant and ask for a warm reply suggesting eight-thirty. The

00:01:20.727 --> 00:01:25.855
assistant prepares wording for staff to review. Use in composer places it

00:01:25.855 --> 00:01:29.700
in a staff message, ready to check and send.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.858
The assistant can also suggest a follow-up and a shift note. Here,

00:01:34.858 --> 00:01:39.365
staff keeps a reminder about the quiet table and a note to

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:43.873
check the allergy with the guest and kitchen. Save the enquiry to

00:01:43.873 --> 00:01:45.000
retain these changes.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:50.702
Add the staff suggestion, then Alex's acceptance. Eight-thirty is now the agreed

00:01:50.702 --> 00:01:55.753
time in the brief. Open Time to read the messages supporting it,

00:01:55.753 --> 00:01:58.700
including the offer and the guest's yes.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:04.661
If a message or speaker was entered incorrectly, edit it directly. FormBridge

00:02:04.661 --> 00:02:09.972
rebuilds the brief from the corrected conversation and asks staff to review

00:02:09.972 --> 00:02:11.300
the result again.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:17.573
Find guest requests in Guest care. Each suggestion comes with the customer's

00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:23.196
words. Keep Alex's name, birthday, quiet table and peanut allergy after reviewing

00:02:23.196 --> 00:02:28.350
them. Dietary arrangements still need checking with the guest and kitchen.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.418
With all five booking details ready, staff approves the brief. The desk

00:02:34.418 --> 00:02:39.836
offers a downloadable brief, JSON and a calendar reminder. Approval prepares the

00:02:39.836 --> 00:02:43.900
request for handoff; it does not reserve a table.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:48.817
Give the enquiry a useful name. Save it on this device, or

00:02:48.817 --> 00:02:53.083
choose the private Juniper House team. We save Alex's birthday dinner to

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:54.150
the shared desk.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:00.065
The enquiry book brings saved cases back into view. Search by a

00:03:00.065 --> 00:03:05.329
useful name, reopen the conversation, or bring back a JSON export. This

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:08.400
device and team enquiries have separate locations.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:14.000
Open Service planner and choose the thirteenth of November. Alex's enquiry appears

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.950
at eight-thirty with six guests, the birthday and dietary request. Staff can

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.250
copy or download a handoff for the shift.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.480
Switch to Follow-ups. The reminder is due today and says exactly what

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.060
needs doing. Open the enquiry to continue, or mark the task done

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.350
once the real work is complete.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.855
The team desk holds the same saved enquiry. Set Under review, a

00:03:39.855 --> 00:03:44.709
high priority and an owner. Give the next step an exact due

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:48.350
time, with an escalation interval if it becomes overdue.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.533
Add a team comment so the next shift knows what to check.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:58.067
Staff notes and comments stay in the team workspace, separate from the

00:03:58.067 --> 00:03:59.200
guest's review page.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:05.479
Create a private guest review link. Alex sees the date, time, guest

00:04:05.479 --> 00:04:11.109
count and preferences, and can send a correction or confirm the request.

00:04:11.109 --> 00:04:15.800
The page explains that a restaurant reservation still needs confirmation.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:20.572
Alex submits the review and receives a receipt. The team can pick

00:04:20.572 --> 00:04:24.350
up the response in its inbox before taking the next step.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.880
The guest book keeps reviewed guest records and enquiry history together. Staff

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.760
should check that a record belongs to the right person, and confirm

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.200
past preferences before using them again.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:43.229
In Restaurant library, the team maintains the facts guests can ask about.

00:04:43.229 --> 00:04:48.607
Here, approved dinner hours include the kitchen closing time. Publish only information

00:04:48.607 --> 00:04:50.400
your restaurant has checked.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.990
Open the branded guest page or copy the website widget code. Guests

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:00.930
can ask questions and prepare an enquiry, with contact details and consent

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.400
before sending it to the team.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:09.498
Ask when dinner is served. The guest assistant shows Juniper House's approved

00:05:09.498 --> 00:05:14.946
hours and their source. Particular requests are passed to the team for

00:05:14.946 --> 00:05:15.400
checking.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:21.485
The email and WhatsApp connections are simulated. Here, a follow-up email reaches

00:05:21.485 --> 00:05:26.921
Alex's existing enquiry. Staff asks for a reply draft, checks the wording

00:05:26.921 --> 00:05:31.450
and sends a simulated response. No real guest is contacted.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:38.529
Connections also offers reservation handoff simulations. Select an approved, saved enquiry and

00:05:38.529 --> 00:05:44.957
check the simulated availability. This lets the team explore the workflow without

00:05:44.957 --> 00:05:47.100
contacting a booking platform.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:53.729
The simulated handoff returns a reference and a cancellation control. Its status

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:59.707
stays clearly labelled. In real service, the restaurant must still make and

00:05:59.707 --> 00:06:01.700
confirm the actual reservation.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:07.750
From the first message to the next shift: a conversation, a reviewable

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:13.150
brief, useful assistance and a team that knows the next step. Open

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.850
FormBridge and bring your own enquiry.
